// dimension lld must be large enough for the local allocation on the calling rank.
// The grid object, when non-NULL, must outlive the descriptor. Redistribution
// routines (cublasMpGemr2D and cublasMpTrmr2D) also allow grid == NULL on
// ranks that do not participate in that matrix's process grid.
//
//   - m: in Number of rows in the global matrix
//   - n: in Number of columns in the global matrix
//   - mb: in Positive blocking factor used to distribute the rows of the global matrix
//   - nb: in Positive blocking factor used to distribute the columns of the global matrix
//   - rsrc: in Row rank of the process that owns the first row block of the global matrix. When grid is non-NULL, must satisfy 0 <= rsrc < grid->nprow
//   - csrc: in Column rank of the process that owns the first column block of the global matrix. When grid is non-NULL, must satisfy 0 <= csrc < grid->npcol
//   - lld: in Positive leading dimension of the local matrix. It must be large enough for the local allocation on the calling rank
//   - type_: in Data type of the matrix (e.g., CUDA_R_32F, CUDA_R_64F, CUDA_R_16F, CUDA_R_16BF, CUDA_R_8F_E4M3, CUDA_R_8F_E5M2, CUDA_R_4F_E2M1, CUDA_R_8I, CUDA_R_32I, CUDA_C_32F, CUDA_C_64F)
